<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46914" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sŭper-vĕhor</span></b> , vectus,
		3, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. dep.
				n.</i>, <i>to go</i>, <i>ride</i>,
				<i>sail</i>, etc., <i>over</i> or
				<i>past</i> (very rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">montem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cat.
					66, 43</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">promontorium Calabriae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					42, 48, 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">arma tua,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aus. Epigr. 24, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">eos universos montibus harenarum supervectis
					operuisse,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell. 16, 11, 8</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To ride</i>, <i>ride upon</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pullo asinae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ambros. in Luc. 8, 59</span></i>
			.</div>
